    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nThe steady-state plasma concentration is calculated as infusion rate divided by clearance: \\( C_{ss} = \\frac{1.6 \\text{ mg/min}}{640 \\text{ mL/min}} = 0.0025 \\text{ mg/mL} \\). Among the options, 0.002 mg/mL (option A) is the closest match, as the half-life is an unnecessary distractor.",
