      "generated_answer": "The data show that while margin status and T-stage influence local recurrence rates, the differences are not statistically significant (P = ns), and even with negative margins, the local failure rate is substantial (40% for T1-T2 tumors). This suggests that neither margin status nor T-stage reliably predict local control in buccal mucosa cancer when treated with surgery alone. Therefore, the evidence does not support them as accurate predictors.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
