    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Depth First Search (DFS) can get stuck in a blind alley, especially in infinite or very deep search spaces, because it explores as deeply as possible along each branch before backtracking. If it chooses a path that leads nowhere (a dead end), it must backtrack all the way to a previous node to try another option. In contrast, BFS explores level by level and is guaranteed to find solutions in finite spaces without getting permanently stuck.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
