      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCoins(prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    # dp[i] represents the minimum coins needed to acquire fruits from index i to n-1 (0-indexed)\n    # We'll use 1-indexed logic internally, so fruit at index i corresponds to position i+1\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[n] = 0  # Base case: no fruits left to acquire\n    \n    # Process from the last fruit backwards to the first\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        # If we purchase fruit at position i (0-indexed), which is the (i+1)-th fruit\n        # We get the next (i+1) fruits for free, so we can skip up to i + (i+1) = 2*i + 1\n        # The next fruit we might need to purchase is at position (i + (i+1)) = 2*i + 1 (0-indexed)\n        # But we need to consider all possible next purchase points from i+1 to min(n, 2*i+2)\n        next_free_end = i + (i + 1) + 1  # 1-indexed: we get next (i+1) fruits, so free up to position (i+1) + (i+1) = 2*i+2\n        for j in range(i + 1, min(n + 1, next_free_end + 1)):\n            dp[i] = min(dp[i], prices[i] + dp[j])\n    \n    return dp[0]\n```",
