      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maxSumOfSquares(nums, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    # count how many numbers have each bit set (bits 0..30)\n    cnt = [0] * 31\n    for num in nums:\n        for b in range(31):\n            if num >> b & 1:\n                cnt[b] += 1\n\n    # top will hold the values of the k numbers we are building\n    top = [0] * k\n\n    # process bits from most significant to least\n    for b in range(30, -1, -1):\n        take = min(cnt[b], k)\n        if take == 0:\n            continue\n        val = 1 << b\n        # assign this bit to the 'take' largest numbers (first 'take' in descending order)\n        for i in range(take):\n            top[i] += val\n\n    # sum of squares of the k largest numbers modulo 1e9+7\n    ans = 0\n    for v in top:\n        ans = (ans + v * v) % MOD\n    return ans\n```",
