      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n    \n    # Build tree and compute depths\n    parent = [0] * (N + 1)\n    children = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    \n    for i in range(2, N + 1):\n        p = int(next(it))\n        parent[i] = p\n        children[p].append(i)\n    \n    # Compute depths using BFS\n    depth = [0] * (N + 1)\n    depth[1] = 0\n    queue = deque([1])\n    while queue:\n        u = queue.popleft()\n        for v in children[u]:\n            depth[v] = depth[u] + 1\n            queue.append(v)\n    \n    # For each person, track the maximum coverage depth\n    max_coverage = [0] * (N + 1)\n    \n    # Process each insurance\n    for _ in range(M):\n        x = int(next(it))\n        y = int(next(it))\n        # Update coverage for person x and their descendants\n        # For person i, coverage is valid if depth[i] - depth[x] <= y\n        # => depth[i] <= depth[x] + y\n        # So we want to mark all descendants within y generations\n        # Instead of traversing each time, we store the max allowed depth\n        max_coverage[x] = max(max_coverage[x], depth[x] + y)\n    \n    # BFS to propagate coverage and count covered people\n    covered = [False] * (N + 1)\n    queue = deque()\n    \n    # Initialize queue with people who have coverage\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        if max_coverage[i] > 0:\n            queue.append(i)\n            covered[i] = True\n    \n    while queue:\n        u = queue.popleft()\n        for v in children[u]:\n            # v is covered if max_coverage[u] >= depth[v]\n            if max_coverage[u] >= depth[v] and not covered[v]:\n                covered[v] = True\n                queue.append(v)\n    \n    # Count covered people\n    count = sum(1 for i in range(1, N + 1) if covered[i])\n    print(count)\n\nsolve()\n```",
