    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_405",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nThere is a grid of H rows and W columns, each cell having a side length of 1, and we have N tiles.\nThe i-th tile (1\\leq i\\leq N) is a rectangle of size A_i\\times B_i.\nDetermine whether it is possible to place the tiles on the grid so that all of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- Every cell is covered by exactly one tile.\n- It is fine to have unused tiles.\n- The tiles may be rotated or flipped when placed. However, each tile must be aligned with the edges of the cells without extending outside the grid.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN H W\nA_1 B_1\nA_2 B_2\n\\ldots\nA_N B_N\n\nOutput\n\nIf it is possible to place the tiles on the grid so that all of the conditions in the problem statement are satisfied, print Yes; otherwise, print No.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1\\leq N\\leq 7\n- 1 \\leq H,W \\leq 10\n- 1\\leq A_i,B_i\\leq 10\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n5 5 5\n1 1\n3 3\n4 4\n2 3\n2 5\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\n\nPlacing the 2-nd, 4-th, and 5-th tiles as shown below covers every cell of the grid by exactly one tile.\n\nHence, print Yes.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n1 1 2\n2 3\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\n\nIt is impossible to place the tile without letting it extend outside the grid.\nHence, print No.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n1 2 2\n1 1\n\nSample Output 3\n\nNo\n\nIt is impossible to cover all cells with the tile.\nHence, print No.\n\nSample Input 4\n\n5 3 3\n1 1\n2 2\n2 2\n2 2\n2 2\n\nSample Output 4\n\nNo\n\nNote that each cell must be covered by exactly one tile.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to determine if I can cover an H×W grid exactly using some subset of N tiles (each tile can be rotated), where each tile is a rectangle of size A_i × B_i.\n\nGiven the constraints (N ≤ 7, H,W ≤ 10), I can use a backtracking/DFS approach:\n1. Try to place each tile in every possible position and orientation on the grid\n2. Use recursion to try placing one tile at a time\n3. If I can cover all cells exactly once, return \"Yes\"\n4. If no combination works, return \"No\"\n\nThe key insights:\n- Each tile can be placed in two orientations: A_i×B_i or B_i×A_i\n- I need to cover every cell exactly once (no overlaps, no gaps)\n- I can leave some tiles unused\n- The grid has H rows and W columns\n\nI'll use a 2D array to represent the grid state (0 = empty, 1 = occupied)\nThen recursively try placing each unused tile in every possible position and orientation.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    line = sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()\n    N = int(line[0])\n    H = int(line[1])\n    W = int(line[2])\n    \n    tiles = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        line = sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()\n        A = int(line[0])\n        B = int(line[1])\n        tiles.append((A, B))\n    \n    # Create grid representation (H rows, W columns)\n    # 0 means empty, 1 means occupied\n    grid = [[0] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    # Try to place tiles using DFS/backtracking\n    def can_place_tile(row, col, height, width):\n        # Check if tile of size height×width can be placed at (row, col)\n        if row + height > H or col + width > W:\n            return False\n        for i in range(row, row + height):\n            for j in range(col, col + width):\n                if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                    return False\n        return True\n    \n    def place_tile(row, col, height, width, place=True):\n        # Place or remove tile at position (row, col) with dimensions height×width\n        for i in range(row, row + height):\n            for j in range(col, col + width):\n                grid[i][j] = 1 if place else 0\n    \n    def dfs(tile_index):\n        # If all tiles have been considered\n        if tile_index == N:\n            # Check if grid is completely filled\n            for i in range(H):\n                for j in range(W):\n                    if grid[i][j] == 0:\n                        return False\n            return True\n        \n        # Try not using the current tile\n        if dfs(tile_index + 1):\n            return True\n        \n        # Try using the current tile in both orientations\n        A, B = tiles[tile_index]\n        \n        # Orientation 1: A × B\n        for i in range(H):\n            for j in range(W):\n                if can_place_tile(i, j, A, B):\n                    place_tile(i, j, A, B, True)\n                    if dfs(tile_index + 1):\n                        return True\n                    place_tile(i, j, A, B, False)  # backtrack\n        \n        # Orientation 2: B × A (rotated)\n        for i in range(H):\n            for j in range(W):\n                if can_place_tile(i, j, B, A):\n                    place_tile(i, j, B, A, True)\n                    if dfs(tile_index + 1):\n                        return True\n                    place_tile(i, j, B, A, False)  # backtrack\n        \n        return False\n    \n    # Start DFS from tile 0\n    if dfs(0):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
