    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import permutations\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it)); H = int(next(it)); W = int(next(it))\n    \n    tiles = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        a = int(next(it)); b = int(next(it))\n        tiles.append((a, b))\n    \n    total_area = H * W\n    \n    # Try all subsets and permutations of tiles\n    # Since N <= 7, we can try all subsets (2^7 = 128) and permutations (up to 7! = 5040)\n    \n    # Precompute all possible orientations for each tile\n    tile_orientations = []\n    for a, b in tiles:\n        if a == b:\n            tile_orientations.append([(a, b)])\n        else:\n            tile_orientations.append([(a, b), (b, a)])\n    \n    # Try all subsets of tiles\n    for mask in range(1, 1 << N):\n        subset = []\n        for i in range(N):\n            if mask & (1 << i):\n                subset.append(i)\n        \n        # Check if total area matches\n        area_sum = 0\n        for i in subset:\n            a, b = tiles[i]\n            area_sum += a * b\n        if area_sum != total_area:\n            continue\n        \n        # Try all permutations of the subset\n        for perm in permutations(subset):\n            # Try all combinations of orientations\n            orientations = [tile_orientations[i] for i in perm]\n            # Use backtracking to try placing tiles\n            grid = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n            \n            def place_tile(idx, grid):\n                if idx == len(perm):\n                    return True\n                \n                i = perm[idx]\n                a, b = tiles[i]\n                \n                # Try both orientations\n                for (h, w) in orientations[idx]:\n                    # Try all positions\n                    for r in range(H - h + 1):\n                        for c in range(W - w + 1):\n                            # Check if area is free\n                            can_place = True\n                            for dr in range(h):\n                                for dc in range(w):\n                                    if grid[r+dr][c+dc]:\n                                        can_place = False\n                                        break\n                                if not can_place:\n                                    break\n                            \n                            if can_place:\n                                # Place tile\n                                for dr in range(h):\n                                    for dc in range(w):\n                                        grid[r+dr][c+dc] = True\n                                \n                                if place_tile(idx + 1, grid):\n                                    # Backtrack: remove tile\n                                    for dr in range(h):\n                                        for dc in range(w):\n                                            grid[r+dr][c+dc] = False\n                                    return True\n                                \n                                # Backtrack: remove tile\n                                for dr in range(h):\n                                    for dc in range(w):\n                                        grid[r+dr][c+dc] = False\n                \n                return False\n            \n            if place_tile(0, grid):\n                print(\"Yes\")\n                return\n    \n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
