    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The balanced budget multiplier is equal to 1 because when government spending and taxes increase by the same amount, the net effect on equilibrium income is equal to the increase in government spending (since the tax increase reduces consumption by less than the full amount due to the marginal propensity to consume being less than 1). All other multipliers listed are typically greater than 1 (e.g., spending, investment, income, fiscal policy multipliers) or not standard concepts (e.g., inflation, interest rate multipliers), and the long-run aggregate supply curve is vertical (infinite elasticity), not unitary. The money multiplier is usually greater than 1 and depends on reserve ratios.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
