      "generated_answer": "Variance decompositions in VAR models measure the proportion of forecast error variance attributable to shocks from each variable (ii is true), and it is common for a variable’s own shocks to explain most of its forecast error variance (iv is true). However, variance decompositions depend on variable ordering just like impulse responses (iii is false), and they do not measure the impact of a “unit shock” directly—that’s the role of impulse responses (i is false).  \nThus, the correct answer is: $\\boxed{\\text{E}}$",
      "success": true,
