      "generated_answer": "The card shop properly rejected the October 25 delivery because, under UCC § 2-508, a seller may cure a nonconforming delivery only if the time for performance has not yet expired and the buyer is given notice of intent to cure — here, the printing company’s October 15 notice came after the original November 1 deadline, and the card shop had already rejected the nonconforming goods. Since the printing company failed to deliver conforming goods by the agreed date and the card shop had no obligation to accept a late cure, the rejection was valid.  \n$\\boxed{\\text{D}}$",
